# Healthcare requirements (SPOTS)

SPOTS is for children and teens with cancer and their caregivers. Code and copy must respect that context.

## Users & roles
- **Children/teens** — primary users reporting feelings and symptoms
- **Parents/guardians** — oversight; may act in a child context (`family_id` / reporting-as flows)
- **Healthcare team / admins** — clinical or system access; least privilege

## Privacy & compliance mindset
- Treat data as sensitive (HIPAA-like): no secrets in git, no unnecessary PHI in logs, UI copy, or `aria-label`s
- Consider COPPA for users under 13 (parental oversight, careful data collection)
- Secure auth and authorization; fail closed when identity or family context is unclear

## Product UX constraints
- Age-appropriate language and imagery; emotionally sensitive messaging
- Clear feedback for save/error/empty states (not color-only)
- Parent vs child context must stay obvious and safe in the UI

## Built product focus (today)
- Symptom / feeling tracking and reporting to the care team via REDCap-backed APIs
- Do not invent fallbacks or fake clinical data when REDCap/APIs fail
